D6 phase 1 (owner decisions 2026-10-18/19; docs/fonts/embedded-font-rights.md): a PDF's
own embedded simple TrueType fonts are used to lay out and draw its text.

Before, the inline import read each embedded program only to guess the family name and
weight (vcl::Font::identifyFont); the text was then measured and drawn with whatever
that family resolved to (a substitute, or a fallback face). Now:
  - Poppler side (pdfioutdev_gpl.cxx): before an embedded simple TrueType font's first
    updateFont, a `fontCodeMap <fontID> <n> <unicode> <gid> ...` line carries the
    Unicode -> glyph pairs for its 256 codes, from Poppler's own code -> GID map
    (Gfx8BitFont::getCodeToGIDMap, the one it renders with) and the font's ToUnicode.
    A PDF subset's own cmap is keyed by character codes, so the program cannot be used
    as it is.
  - Import side (wrapper.cxx): the program is rebuilt with a (3,1) format-4 cmap from
    those pairs (every table offset and length checked against the buffer; TrueType
    outlines only, 6 required tables, <= 64 tables, <= 64 MB) and registered through
    EmbeddedFontsHelper::addEmbeddedFont under the family name the import writes. So
    layout uses it, an editable output names the real family and embeds nothing (D5),
    and the rights rule is the converter's one (D4 patch: PDF-only outputs 0/8/4,
    editable outputs 0/8, no rights information = usable, Restricted alone never,
    0x100 refuses PDF, 0x200 every output). The temp file name carries the program's
    SHA-256 (WAF #594 F2), because addEmbeddedFont keeps an existing file unchecked and
    the rights differ by output; with no hash backend the font is not used.
  - Per document, the parse retains at most 256 programs and 128 MB (both copies
    counted; WAF #594 F1); past either limit a font is not used, with a `[PDFFONT]`
    line. The corpus's largest is 25 programs and 3.1 MB. Transient copies put the peak
    at about 2-3x the figure; what outlives the document is bounded by the driver giving
    each font-carrying document its own engine (#594 F3).
  - Each program is first registered under an internal name of its own
    ("<family> pdf<id>", rights checked there) and the import measures its ascent with
    it, so the metric is the real face's; the document's text never names it.
  - At the end of the parse (~Parser) each face's programs are MERGED into one font
    (pdffont::mergeSubsets: union of the characters; glyf/loca/hmtx rebuilt, composite
    components remapped, long loca, post format 3) when they are subsets of one font
    (same unitsPerEm, identical fpgm/prep/cvt, identical glyphs for shared characters:
    simple ones byte for byte, composites through their components), and registered under
    the family name. The first program keeps its glyph ids, so a composite stored before
    its components (Cairo's order) needs no remapping. Otherwise the program with the
    most characters is used and the others' characters fall back to the D3 substitute,
    never a box. Layout happens after the parse.
  - CID TrueType (phase 2) and CFF programs (phase 3) are not passed yet: their code
    map record is never written, so nothing changes for them.
  - One `[PDFFONT]` line per font on stderr says what happened.
  - Untrusted input: the tables' lengths may not add up to more than the program (so
    overlapping entries cannot multiply its size), each program is parsed once, and the
    shared-glyph comparison stops after 65535 proven pairs per program. A
    program with no family name is not registered under the import's "Arial" fallback.
    The end-of-parse registration runs from ~Parser and catches every exception.
  - A family name containing # ? % is not used: addEmbeddedFont opens its temporary file
    by URL, which osl refuses for # and ? (no corpus PDF has one).
WASM only (#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__ on the import side; the Poppler record is only read by
it). Routed to pdf-docx and pdf-pptx by the pdfimport-inline arm.

