+// keeps an existing file unchecked, and rights differ by output, so a file from another
+// document or another program must never match. Same name now means same bytes; the same
+// bytes under another document's rights never meet in one engine, because the driver gives
+// every document that may carry fonts its own engine (#594 F3; the MCP runs one engine
